Tavletta's print server for Debian
==================================

tavletta-server.service runs `tavletta serve` as the system user tavletta
(made by this package), sandboxed, on 127.0.0.1:8790. It is installed but
neither enabled nor started; an upgrade restarts it if it runs. Its files:

  /etc/tavletta/printers.toml   the printers clients may use
  /etc/tavletta/tokens.toml     the access tokens (hashes)
  /var/lib/tavletta/labels/     the label files

Both TOML files belong to tavletta, mode 600. Make a token as that user:

  sudo -u tavletta /usr/bin/tavletta token new NAME --role print \
      --tokens /etc/tavletta/tokens.toml --printers /etc/tavletta/printers.toml
  sudo systemctl enable --now tavletta-server

The service has no access to devices: it prints to network printers. The
full guide, with a reverse proxy for HTTPS:
https://tavletta.joshuahirsig.xyz/server-install/#package

Purging the package (apt purge tavletta-server) deletes /etc/tavletta with
its printers and tokens, and /var/lib/tavletta unless label files are left
in it. The user tavletta stays, as files may still belong to it (Debian
does not remove system users on purge); remove it with `deluser tavletta`.
